               <head>Miscellany of magical texts</head>
               <msContents>
                  <summary>A miscellany of magical texts in several Maghribī hands, on loose leaves
                     of various sizes, now out of order. It contains magic squares; geomantic
                     tableaux; talismanic designs; a short treatise on the names and figures of
                     angels; instructions for amulets and talismans; small folded sheets, probably
                     once used as amulets; and several astrological tables (the months in their
                     Maghribi forms with their zodiac signs, the lunar mansions marked auspicious,
                     inauspicious or mixed, and the planets). No title, author or date.</summary>
                  <msItem xml:id="UOL_MS_289-item1">
                     <title type="desc" xml:lang="en">Miscellany of magical texts</title>
                     <colophon>One leaf is signed <quote xml:lang="ar">كاتبه محمد بن رمضان</quote>
                           (<persName role="scr" key="">Muḥammad ibn Ramaḍān</persName>).
                        Undated.</colophon>
                     <note>
                        <p>Two sheets showing angels with their names (e.g. Gabriel) were added from
                           MS 284 in 2023.</p>
                     </note>
                     <textLang mainLang="ar">Arabic</textLang>
                  </msItem>
               </msContents>
